A||||17||BC-GT||Front licence plate impeding airflow to radiator||||1||
Z||000000||BC-GT||06-24-2001||08:09 PM||||Here in BC we are required by law to have a front plate but I hate it. I remember reading about someone taking a case like this to court or something saying it interfered with the working of the car because it impedes the main airflow(intake) to the rad or something to that effect. Does anyone know how it turned out?<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-24-2001||08:27 PM||||nice try, but I dont think itll work. there gonna get their money anyway. You hear the one about the guy that was speeding and his excuse was he just washed it and was blow drying it.......than didnt work either.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||06-24-2001||09:00 PM||||You have seen the mug shots of the guy with no front plate.  He has a number on his shirt.<BR>In NY state front plates are mandatory and, I have not had any cooling problems in 14 years of driving my Fiero.  A lot of air gets deflected by the air dam under the front of the car,||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||06-24-2001||09:05 PM||||I thought this too but I heard the Fiero draws the air for the radiator from under the car.  <P>It's a law here in MD too but I still dont have mine.  Here is what I do.  I carry around the plate, and the bracket.  I have been pulled over twice, and each time I say "oh I finally got a bracket for it and I was just going to install it, but I can do it now if you want me to" and both times they said "yes do it now"  So I threw it on for the time being, then when I got home I took it off.  It looks like crap IMHO.  Even if the same cops pull me over again for not having it, by law they can't fine me the first time, even though its not my first time, but they never gave me a "formal, written" warning so it will be the first time technically.  Until I get that written warning I am not putting it on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BC-GT||06-24-2001||09:36 PM||||Well dagnabbit, it sure sounded like a good excuse. What we need is one of the original Fiero designers in court saying "yes, your honor, that hole in the front of the car is for cooling the rad"||||reg||1
Z||000005||sjp777||06-24-2001||10:31 PM||||I've had GT nose fieros for 10 years and have never had the front plate on.<P>I have never gotten pulled over or issued a ticket for it.<P>I think that is one of those stupid no reason for laws that cops usually don't enforce because they should and usually do have better things to do.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrgone||06-24-2001||11:08 PM||||setting it on the dash too much to ask?||||reg||1
Z||000007||BC-GT||06-24-2001||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>setting it on the dash too much to ask?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I would rather have it on the bumper than the dash myself.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||06-24-2001||11:37 PM||||The reason the cop told me was "In a hit and run, the front plate is the first thing to fall off" which is a good reason.  But I think the true reason is for speed traps.  It's a flat, easy target.  ||||reg||12
Z||000009||rogergarrison||06-25-2001||12:22 AM||||yes black88gt, a friend of mine whos a sheriff told me that too about being the radar target point. thats why ohio wont get rid of front plates.<P>those radar defuser covers are illegal here too, but to get all the help I can, my front plate is laid over at an angle towards the ground. Dont know if that works at all, but Ill try anything thats not totally stupid. You can still easily read it, but I hope it reflects some of the signals down instead of back to thier gun.(yes I do know that aluminum foil is dumb   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">...)<P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroPerformance||06-25-2001||01:01 AM||||I live in Ohio where it is manditory. Almost every other car on the road doesn't have one though. I didn't like the way it looked so I took it off. That was at least 6 months ago. Since then I've been pulled over once (unrelated to the missing plate) and the cop didn't even say anything about that plate. I haven't had any problems with it... I've even been on the police "hot list" of people to look for speeding and still nothing about the plate. If you don't like it I say ditch it. Keep it in your trunk tho and if you do run into a problem say you hit an animal and it fell off and you are waiting for a new mount from the FieroStore.<P><BR>disclaimer: I am in no way forcing or suggesting that anyone break any laws.<P>heh<BR>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierospeeder||06-25-2001||01:34 AM||||I got pulled over about 4 months ago in my tbird turbo 87.  for not having a front plate, i told the officer i have no bracket to hold the plate.  He told me i had to go to the dealership and get one.  "verbal warning" in illinois.<P>I havn't gone to the dealership yet, but finding my car in the junkyard is almost impossible and all the ones i found have the front bumper"nose" taken off. I can put my plate on but i would have to bend it in a 45 degree angle to fit my bumper.<P>And in illinois, i see so many people without front plates on sports cars and on getto cars. <P>The way the air gets in the radiator is by the air dam creating a low pressure? area behind the air dam, causing the air to go through the radiator.||||reg||1
Z||000012||hyhy4u||06-25-2001||08:55 PM||||I think the Aero nose looks terrible with a plate, so i just leave it off and keep the plate in my car in case i ever get pulled over for it...but never had a problem yet.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Toddster||06-25-2001||09:04 PM||||If your engine is running hot living in BC then I think the problem is something else!<P>BUT...if you want, you can cut holes in your license plate around the letters.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BC-GT||06-25-2001||09:12 PM||||Toddster, my car actually runs cool, I just hate the front plate and would like a legal leg to stand on if I decided to take it off and got pulled over.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DecadenceR||06-25-2001||10:32 PM||||Here in NJ you have to have both plates too. <BR>My friend had a newer camaro with the little bowtie ebhind the plate. So he left it off. He was fine in my town. he started working the next town over, and they busted him every chance they got. I guess it all depends on the cops in your area and how big of a prick they can be. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Tina||06-25-2001||10:50 PM||||Seem to remember that somebody here on the forum had a simular problem.<P>Went one step further though.<BR>Actually went to court,and fought the ticket.<BR>The defense: Front license plate holder discontinued.<BR>I believe he got out of the ticket <P>Gotta love those success story's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
